openstack-horizon — OpenStack Dashboard (Horizon) 27.0.0 (2026.2 Hibiscus)
============================================================================

This package installs the Horizon dashboard: the Django project
openstack_dashboard plus the openstack_auth Keystone backend, served
by gunicorn. It installs software ONLY: nothing is enabled, started,
migrated or credentialed at install time.

What it ships
-------------

  openstack_dashboard.wsgi:application   the supported WSGI application
  /etc/horizon/local/local_settings.py.example   operator settings template
  /usr/share/horizon/conf            generator/policy inputs
  /etc/init.d/horizon                OpenRC service (gunicorn)
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/horizon.service   systemd service (gunicorn)
  /etc/conf.d/horizon                WSGI container runtime settings

Operator steps (NOT performed by this package)
----------------------------------------------

1. Write the Django settings from the example (SECRET_KEY, Keystone
   endpoints, database, session backend, static root, ...):

     cp /etc/horizon/local/local_settings.py.example \
        /etc/horizon/local/local_settings.py
     # edit /etc/horizon/local/local_settings.py
     #
     # /etc/horizon is on the service PYTHONPATH, so upgrades to this
     # package never clobber the operator's file.

2. Collect static assets into the operator-chosen static root
   (served by nginx in production, never by gunicorn):

     DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=openstack_dashboard.settings \
     PYTHONPATH=/etc/horizon \
     python -m django collectstatic --noinput

3. Initialise the session/auth database (sqlite for trials, MariaDB
   via python-pymysql for real use):

     DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=openstack_dashboard.settings \
     PYTHONPATH=/etc/horizon \
     python -m django migrate --noinput

4. Enable and start the service explicitly:

     rc-update add horizon default && rc-service horizon start
     # or
     systemctl enable --now horizon

Horizon authenticates against Keystone; there are no local dashboard
users to create. Front it with nginx/haproxy for TLS and static
files; gunicorn serves only the Django application.

Independence
------------

Horizon depends on the Django stack, XStatic assets and the service
client libraries. It does not run any OpenStack API itself and can be
installed on its own.
